</div><p>(a)</p><div>\(PG = \) [[input:ans1]] cm [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b)</p><div>\(OF = \) [[input:ans2]] cm [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find angle \(XOY\), to the nearest degree.</p><div>[[input:ans3]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Every point on the bisector of an angle is the same distance from both arms, so \(PG = PF = {@a@}\) cm.</p><p>(b) Triangle \(OFP\) has a right angle at \(F\) and hypotenuse \(OP\): \(OF^2 = OP^2 - PF^2 = {@c@}^2 - {@a@}^2 = {@c^2-a^2@}\), so \(OF = {@bb@}\) cm.</p><p>(c) In triangle \(OFP\), \(\sin \angle FOP = \dfrac{PF}{OP} = \dfrac{ {@a@} }{ {@c@} }\), so \(\angle FOP = {@dispdp(float(floor(10^2*(dh)+1/2)/10^2),2)@}^{\circ}\). \(OP\) bisects angle \(XOY\), so \(\angle XOY = 2 \times \angle FOP = {@dispdp(float(floor(10^2*(ang)+1/2)/10^2),2)@}^{\circ}\), which is \({@floor(ang+1/2)@}^{\circ}\) to the nearest degree.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
